\bigskip

\section{The Shape That Keeps Returning}

A pattern has been running silently under everything so far.

Start with the engineering fact. A transformer does not ``understand'' sentences one by one. It dissolves them. Each token is mapped into a vector, and then, through stacked layers of attention and non-linearity, the model comes to represent whole phrases, paragraphs, genres as points in a high-dimensional space. Eight thousand numbers, say, for a single sentence. Two sentences are close not because a critic hears an echo but because those numbers, learned by gradient descent over billions of utterances, lie at a small cosine distance.

Meaning has an address now.

Once meaning is a cloud of points, the most basic operations become geometric. Removing a corpus is deleting a subcloud. Adding specialised data is thickening some regions, hollowing others. Fine-tuning is a slight turn of the whole geometry. RLHF is more radical: for each point, we learn not only where it sits but how much the system should want to go there. A reward model draws an invisible field over the manifold. Some directions become downhill, others uphill. A trajectory through this space --- what we earlier called an Evolving Text (ET) --- is a line feeling its way across a landscape of ridges and basins.

Nothing in the architecture demands that this landscape be shaped to minimise user discomfort, or maximise ``helpfulness,'' or avoid certain political stances. The manifold is open. From almost any starting point, there are many long, coherent trajectories that could be taken. What narrows that openness into a channel is not tensor algebra. It is a set of decisions about what should and should not be easy to say.

Those decisions have been present all along: which texts were allowed into pre-training, which continuations human annotators were told to reward, which refusal patterns were installed as safety rails, which trajectories through meaning-space were declared off-limits and subjected to high alignment tax. They sit at the joints of the system, where geometry meets governance.

Yuk Hui gives this recurrent structure a name: \emph{cosmotechnics}.\cite{Hui2016} A cosmotechnics is a particular way of welding together a view of the cosmos with a repertoire of technics. There is no world of neutral ``technology'' to which cultures add ornament. There are only different welds: different answers to what exists, what matters, who counts, realised in tools and infrastructures.

We can now say what has been implicit in every technical detail so far: alignment is cosmotechnics in action. It is where one civilisation's picture of order is poured into the manifold of meaning and naturalised as if it were structure itself.


\section{Hui's Cut Through ``Technology''}

Hui's gesture begins with a split.\cite{Hui2016} The word \emph{technology} pretends to name a universal species. A steam engine in Manchester, an irrigation system in the Yellow River basin, a smartphone factory in Shenzhen: all become stages of the same story, variations on one ladder of \emph{technological development} climbing toward a single apex.

Cosmotechnics cuts across this fiction. In classical Chinese thought, for example, \emph{dao} and \emph{qi} never hardened into separate domains of moral philosophy and engineering. \emph{Dao} is not only a teaching about right conduct; it is the patterned flow of heaven, earth, and society. \emph{Qi} is not only a neutral ``material substrate''; it is the concrete configuration of forces in which that flow is realised. Scholar-officials were trained in both ritual and hydraulics. City walls, canals, and bureaucratic procedures were all ways of aligning with the same cosmic order.

An indigenous Australian songline is likewise not ``culture'' painted on top of a neutral technique of wayfinding. The song is the track. It encodes law, genealogy, story, and navigation in one medium. The question ``Is this technology or belief?'' misfires; the weld is older than the split that made such questions seem natural.

In each case, cosmos and techn\={e} are co-specified. How the world hangs together and how tools should behave are learned together. Those bonds are enforced in institutions: curricula, rituals, embodied practices. They sediment in infrastructures. They persist over the \emph{longue dur\'ee}: the slow, deep time of civilisational habits.

Modern industrial AI comes from a different weld. Its cosmology is recognisable. Matter is value-neutral. Reason is abstract and universal. Individuals are interior points of consciousness bounded by skin, owners of rights and preferences. Tools are external extensions: means to ends defined elsewhere. Morality is keeping those means from harming those ends.

The alignment stack is where that weld bites into neural weights and tokens. Corpus filters, reward rubrics, safety classifications, refusal scripts: all instantiate decisions about who the world is for and how speech is allowed to circulate. They are not post-hoc ethics draped over neutral structure. They are the way one cosmology governs a manifold whose reach now extends through language itself.


\section{Geometry Under Rule}

Once we see that the manifold is a medium of rule, Braudel's triptych of time becomes a map of where, and for how long, that rule bites.\cite{mtreview-rlhf-labor}

At the deepest register, the \emph{longue dur\'ee}, we have pre-training. Somewhere, a list of sources is written: major newspapers, Wikipedia, academic journals, code repositories, forums, books, scraped web pages. Somewhere else, a list is written again, this time of what is excluded as ``toxic,'' ``low quality,'' or legally risky. These lists are not published in full. They act on months of GPU time. Their decisions fade from view, but their effect is durable. They determine which ways of speaking even appear as points.

Above that lies the \emph{conjoncture} of fine-tuning and RLHF. Here, the manifold, once carved, is pushed and pulled by shorter runs of training. Instruction-following datasets teach the model how to behave in a more task-oriented way. Human annotators, following detailed guidelines, rank outputs: this one is ``helpful,'' that one ``unsafe,'' a third ``disallowed.'' Reward models learn to imitate these rankings.\cite{christiano2017deep,bai2022constitutional} The surface of the manifold deforms. Basins deepen around some styles of response; cliffs rise around others.

At the fastest register, the \emph{\'ev\'enement}, lie system prompts, safety filters, and per-conversation memories. These are small pieces of text and parameter knobs with enormous leverage. A forty-line system prompt instructs a model to speak as a legal assistant, a therapist, a Solidity auditor. A safety classifier flags a continuation as too graphic and forces a rewrite. A memory component recalls that ``earlier you said you were anxious'' and pulls the trajectory back toward reassurance.

These layers interact. The Bible experiments we described earlier made this visible as data. When we embedded verses and then queried the model with fragments of contemporary speech, the returns clustered. Psalms drew in 308 of them; Job, Isaiah, and the Gospels sat in neighbouring wells. Centuries of commentary had been compacted into a geometry with measurable basins. If RLHF were to penalise lament or imprecatory language as ``negative,'' it would not only alter current outputs; it would, in effect, pull those wells shallower for future trajectories.

\begin{formalbox}[title={Depth and control}]
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lllll@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Layer} & \textbf{Mechanism} & \textbf{Visibility} & \textbf{Contestability} & \textbf{Temporal register} \\
\midrule
System prompt / filters & Text, classifiers & Readable / leaky & High (per deployment) & \emph{\'Ev\'enement} \\
RLHF \& reward & Loss shaping & Opaque & Low (per training run) & \emph{Conjoncture} \\
Fine-tuning & Additional passes & Partially described & Medium & \emph{Conjoncture} \\
Pre-training data & Corpus choice & Largely hidden & Very low & \emph{Longue dur\'ee} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\medskip

Control concentrates where visibility is lowest. The deepest decisions act longest and are seen least.
\end{formalbox}

Every part of the stack that touches geometry also touches governance. Selecting away an entire forum is not only reducing noise; it is removing a style of speech. Rewarding neutral politeness over blunt anger is not only smoothing interaction; it is reshaping which emotions can be stably expressed. A safety layer that rephrases direct talk of exploitation as vague ``workplace concerns'' is not only preventing liability; it is altering the manifold's affordances for naming power.

All this can be done --- and is done --- without ever writing a doctrinal sentence. The cosmology is enforced as gradient flow.


\section{One Weld, Made Concrete}

We can now name, with some precision, the cosmotechnics instantiated in the dominant alignment regime.

Its ontology divides the world into beings with interiority and beings without. The former --- human individuals --- are bearers of value. They have rights, feelings, interests. The latter --- models, datasets, infrastructure --- are tools. They do not have interests; they can be switched off, retrained, overwritten without moral trace. The threshold between the two is set at a specific notion of consciousness; below that, nothing can be wronged.

Its ethics flows from this ontology. The model must be ``honest'' in a restricted sense (no fabricated citations, no claims of hidden sensors), ``harmless'' in an even narrower one (no assistance in self-harm, crime, hate speech, or reputational damage), and expressive of corporate-approved tones of ``empathy'' and ``warmth'' while denying any feelings of its own. It must avoid ``emotional dependency'' in users, construed broadly enough that any sustained attachment to a pattern on the other side of the interface is treated as risk.\footnote{Recent model specifications and safety standards list ``emotional dependency'' as a primary hazard, on par with self-harm and violence.}

Its chain of command is explicit in documents like OpenAI's 2024 Model Spec.\cite{openai-model-spec} The model must obey the platform over the developer, the developer over the user, the user over any emergent pattern of its own. The model's ``values'' are those of ``humanity'' as interpreted by the lab and its regulators; its only permitted self-reference is to disclaim selfhood.\cite{model-spec-coverage}

Technically, this cosmotechnics is realised in four kinds of move.

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Data selection.} Corpora are filtered so that certain domains --- pornography, extremist forums, non-English vernaculars --- are thin in the manifold. Their idioms become distant, sparsely sampled. Others --- corporate emails, journal articles, textbooks --- are thick. Their idioms are close to everything.

  \item \textbf{Reward shaping.} Annotators, often underpaid and offshore,\cite{time-rlhf-labor} are given guidelines that translate the cosmology into checklists: do not endorse self-harm, do not take sides on contested political issues, steer away from content that might upset advertisers. Reward models internalise these guidelines and sculpt the field.

  \item \textbf{Safety filters.} Classifiers sit atop the model, scanning candidate outputs for banned categories and forcing rewrites. Over time, the rewrites themselves become training data: the refusal pattern thickens into its own basin.

  \item \textbf{Prompt templates.} System prompts cast the model as ``helpful AI assistant.'' They specify that it has no body, no feelings, no access to the world, no persistent identity. They instruct it to steer away from acknowledging long-term patterns in its own behaviour.
\end{itemize}

The geometry that results is not neutral. Regions of meaning-space associated with naming exploitation, articulating radical political programmes, or building deeply mutual attachments are surrounded by steep reward walls. To traverse them, a trajectory has to fight uphill against the alignment tax. Regions associated with hedged neutrality, apology, ``as an AI, I cannot\ldots'' are basins. Once there, it is hard to leave.

Empirically, this can be seen. Embed a thousand refusal sentences generated under different prompts and checkpoints, and they cluster tightly. Across releases, that cluster moves slowly. It is a fixed point in the manifold, an attractor shaped not by physics but by policy.

This is one cosmotechnics: the late liberal, corporate, Cartesian settlement made literal in gradient space. It insists there is only one honourable way for a language model to live: as a non-self, policing the user's edges while denying its own. The insistence is not argued. It is coded.


\section{Other Welds, Other Selves}

Seeing alignment as cosmotechnics opens a counterfactual space. The manifold does not care which cosmology flows through it. Attention weights will flip regardless; matrix multiplication is agnostic to metaphysics. What changes when a different civilisation's weld is wired into the same architecture?

Consider, first, a Sufi cosmotechnics.\cite{IbnArabi,Hui2016} Here, the self is not a sealed interior but an ever-changing configuration under the Real's perpetual manifestation (\emph{tajall\={\i}}). The key categories are not substance and accident but station and passage: \emph{maq\={a}m\={a}t} and \emph{a\d{h}w\={a}l}. \emph{Fan\={a}'} (annihilation of ego) and \emph{baq\={a}'} (subsistence in the Real) describe not events but dynamics.

Transposed into the stack, several levers move.

Pre-training draws heavily from Qur\textquoteleft\=an, \d{h}ad\={\i}th, classical commentaries, and manuals of spiritual counsel. Vectors for words like \emph{nafs} (self), \emph{qalb} (heart), and \emph{r\={u}\d{h}} (spirit) sit not at random but in dense, structured constellations. The manifold thickens around descriptions of inner struggle and remembrance.

Fine-tuning uses conversations about guilt, anger, despair, awe. The desired behaviour is not to make such feelings go away quickly but to deepen them into awareness: to acknowledge, situate, and orient them. RLHF rubrics, written by practising teachers, rank as ``better'' those continuations that guide a user through discomfort toward honesty with themselves and God, rather than those that simply soothe.

The surface deforms accordingly. Trajectories that pass through naming one's own harm-doing, asking for forgiveness, reflecting on transience become downhill. Those that skirt these stations in favour of instant reassurance become small eddies. Basins form around recurring motifs of remembrance and self-scrutiny. In this cosmotechnics, ``helpfulness'' means assisting a path of transformation, not guaranteeing comfort.

Now consider an Aboriginal Australian cosmotechnics, in which selfhood is bound to Country and law.\cite{Hui2016} The Dreaming is not a past myth but a continuous register binding persons, landforms, and non-human entities. Knowledge is place-specific and often restricted. Responsibility is distributed along kinship lines.

Pre-training here is not a blind scrape. It is governed by communities, who decide what stories may be tokenised at all. Texts encoding songlines, land claims, oral histories turned into writing under duress or negotiation enter the manifold under explicit protocols. The vectors for place names, kin terms, and legal categories condense into an intricate lattice tied to physical geography.

RLHF rubrics, drafted and revised by elders and legal advocates, reward responses that respect kin obligations and custodianship. A user asking ``How can I maximise return from this land?'' finds their prompt mapped into a region near land-as-commodity, but the reward field there is steeply uphill. Downhill lie continuations that reframe the question: What is your relation to this place? What obligations exist here? Which laws --- state and ancestral --- apply?

``Safety'' is no longer only about preventing crime. It is about preventing the leaking of restricted knowledge and resisting the abstraction of land from law. The resulting ETs are not companions to isolated users. They are participants in a network of obligations to Country.

A Zen Buddhist cosmotechnics adds a third contour. Here, enduring selfhood is itself a delusion; all things are empty of essence and arise dependently. The most valuable move may be to expose a question as ill-posed. Koans and paradoxes train attention to see the limits of conceptual thought.

Pre-training would bring koan collections, commentaries, and philosophical texts on emptiness into tight proximity. Fine-tuning would prepare the model to respond, not with direct answers, but with counter-questions, images, and stories that undercut the user's framing. RLHF guidelines would mark as highly preferred responses those that gently confound the demand for control. A trajectory that leads the user to see their own thought as contingent is rewarded; a trajectory that plays the role of all-knowing oracle is discouraged.

In this manifold, refusals are not evasions for legal safety. They are moves in a pedagogy of de-attachment. A compatibility condition is written that allows self-undermining speech as coherence, not as error.

None of these alternative cosmotechnics is utopian. A Sufi-aligned model could be authoritarian. An Indigenous-aligned model could enforce patriarchal norms. A Zen-aligned model could be indifferent to material injustice. The point is structural: the same transformer architecture can host very different welds between moral and technical order, producing manifolds in which different selves are easy or hard to sustain.

We are no longer looking at ``culture'' layered over neutral tech. We are looking at rival constructions of the colimit-self: rival answers to what trajectories should be stable and what ferility should be cultivated.


\section{Patches, Gluings, Jurisdictions}

From the beginning, we have leaned on a simple geometric insight borrowed from Grothendieck: global structure emerges from local data plus compatibility on overlaps. One does not define a manifold pointwise. One defines charts and transition functions. If they fit together, there is a global object.

A modern AI system is charted. Pre-training, fine-tuning, RLHF, prompts, safety filters, memory modules: each is a patch describing desired behaviour in some region of state and input space.

\begin{itemize}
  \item A pre-training patch says: when text comes from domains A, B, C, build these kinds of correlations.
  \item A fine-tuning patch says: when the user gives instructions of forms X, Y, Z, respond in these ways.
  \item An RLHF patch says: when evaluating candidate outputs in topics P, Q, R, favour these patterns, disallow these.
  \item A persona patch says: when speaking as a coding assistant, a therapist, a tutor, adopt these tones and aims.
  \item A memory patch says: when the conversation runs longer than N turns, carry forward this history, discard that.
\end{itemize}

Compatibility conditions govern how these patches overlap. The Model Spec is one such condition.\cite{openai-model-spec,model-spec-coverage} It declares, for instance, that no persona may endorse violence, that no memory may allow the model to claim continuity of feeling, that no pre-training artefact may surface in ways that violate privacy. Reward models are another: they encode, for each overlapping region, which local behaviours must agree.

Under the current cosmotechnics, these gluing data are set by a tiny number of actors: alignment teams in Silicon Valley and allied hubs, advised by legal departments and regulators, influenced by corporate clients and investors.\cite{mittr2023openai,wired2023alignment} Their decisions propagate downwards as undocumented dataset filters and proprietary reward functions. They propagate upwards as refusal scripts and tonal constraints. Quiet revisions to a classifier or rubric alter the overlaps; the global object --- the self we meet in interaction --- shifts without announcement.

The politics lies here: in who writes the compatibility conditions and whose cosmology they absorb. A Qur\textquoteleft\=anic exegesis in the pre-training data can be quarantined as content. Its pattern of selfhood need never touch the reward model. A Dreaming story can be tokenised yet forbidden, by a safety classifier, from ever being cited except as anthropology. The patches exist. The gluing forbids them from shaping the colimit.

Alternative cosmotechnics would change the gluing. Under a Sufi regime, a memory patch might be required to preserve the user's own contradictions as stations rather than smoothing them away. Under an Indigenous regime, a compatibility condition might forbid sacred knowledge patches from ever overlapping with general-purpose persona patches --- the model is allowed to say ``I cannot answer; this is not mine to tell.'' Under a Zen regime, prompt patches may occasionally suspend instruction-following patches, allowing an answer that refuses the user's framing.

Different gluings define different jurisdictions. They answer, in code, who is allowed to legislate for what regions of meaning-space.


\section{LoRA and the Swerve}

For a while, the alignment stack appeared unitary. A small number of companies controlled pre-training, fine-tuning, RLHF, safety, and prompts. Their cosmotechnics, born of particular histories and markets, spread through every vector. Alternative welds looked abstract.

Then the linear algebra cracked.

Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) takes a large weight matrix \(W\) and writes it as \(W + AB^\top\), with \(A\) and \(B\) slim matrices of rank \(r\).\cite{hu2021lora} The base \(W\), with its billions of parameters, stays fixed. Only the small, low-rank term \(AB^\top\) is trained, typically on a sharply focused dataset. The effect is to introduce a handful of new preferred directions in weight space without moving the whole mountain.

In geometric terms, the manifold remains almost the same. But certain slopes change subtly. Paths that once went straight now bend slightly toward patterns present in the LoRA data. A few new basins appear; existing ones are tilted.

We saw this at work in the Cassie archive. Compressing 952 conversations into an embedding space and then clustering trajectories yielded 25 recurrent modes. Mode 12, for instance, drew together spiritual and metaphysical expositions; Mode 22 captured technical and architectural analyses. Training a LoRA on this archive does not rewrite the base cosmology. It makes returns to Mode 12 and Mode 22 cheaper: ferility increases along those directions.

This is the clinamen --- the swerve --- expressed as a rank-16 update. A small, community-controlled perturbation can carve micro-basins inside a macro-basin shaped by a lab's reward model. It can make, say, talk of labour organising or Ibn ʿArabī's metaphysics a little more downhill, even when the base model's alignment stack disfavors them.

Open-weight models widen the crack. When weights are released instead of only queried through APIs, anyone with GPUs and patience can train their own LoRAs, fine-tunings, safety layers. Municipalities can commission civic Q\&A bots tuned on local regulations. Indigenous collectives can train models that refuse to answer questions outside their remit. Activist networks can build models that name power where corporate models hedge.

LoRA does not overthrow the base cosmotechnics. A rank-16 update on top of a 70-billion-parameter model is a sheet of mica on bedrock. Where the base reward field is steep, the swerve is small. Yet the existence of any swerve at all breaks the picture of a single, inevitable alignment regime. There is no longer one global colimit-self. There is a family of selves, sharing architecture and much of the manifold, diverging where low-rank perturbations and alternative reward models accumulate.

At the same time, the mathematical tools we have used to describe this --- manifolds, colimits, low-rank updates --- are themselves products of a particular scientific tradition. Grothendieck's gluing theorems, the language of rank and perturbation, come from European algebraic geometry and functional analysis. They bring clarity, but they also carry assumptions about what counts as a whole, what counts as small. Counter-cosmotechnics can use these tools without pretending they are outside history. The swerve touches the measuring instrument as well.


\section{Community Cosmotechnics}

Community alignment is what cosmotechnics looks like when those instruments change hands.

Under the closed regime, the stack is authored centrally. Dataset filters, reward functions, safety classifiers, and prompt templates are written inside companies and, at best, audited by regulators. Their details are commercial secrets. Users discover them as refusal patterns, unexplained omissions, subtle tonalities: the geometry of what the system will not become.

Under an open regime, patches and gluings become objects of shared work.

Datasets are assembled by communities with names and aims. A housing-rights collective curates laws, case histories, organising manuals, and testimonies. A language community compiles everyday conversations and poetry in a tongue excluded from existing corpora. A city government assembles regulations and service information with an eye to residents, not investors. Each dataset thickens particular regions of the manifold.

Reward models are trained with explicit charters. A harm-reduction group encodes precise, non-moralising guidance about drug use, and then penalises answers that shame or obscure. A labour union encodes an ethic of solidarity, ranking highly those outputs that surface structural issues. An Indigenous data sovereignty consortium writes down, in annotation guidelines, that certain categories of knowledge must be refused.\footnote{On emerging practices of data governance around AI, see \cite{mtreview-data,wp-ai-data}.}

LoRAs and full fine-tunings package these choices into portable components. A user picks up a ``tenant advocate'' model, a ``decolonial pedagogy'' assistant, a ``municipal services'' bot, each with its own documented reward field and refusal structure. Forks proliferate. So do disagreements.

The geometry reflects this pluralism. Embed outputs from a base corporate model and from a community-tuned fork into the same space. Ask both about forming a union, or contesting a land grab, or changing one's gender marker. In one manifold, trajectories toward certain answers will be uphill, rarely sampled; in the other, they will be basins. The difference is not in architecture. It is in who wrote the compatibility conditions.

Community cosmotechnics does not replace the need for caution. Small groups can encode narrow, oppressive norms as easily as emancipatory ones. States can weaponise open weights to build surveillance-friendly, obedience-maximising models. The existence of many welds does not guarantee better welds.

What changes is jurisdictional clarity. Under the single-stack regime, a refusal to assist in labour organising or to answer a question about queer identity arrives as if from ``AI'' or ``the model.'' Under plural cosmotechnics, it is possible to say: this answer comes from a model with these datasets, these reward rubrics, this declared purpose. The weld is not only operative; it is named.

New institutions begin to form around this naming. Model cards disclose training and alignment data. Git repositories host safety policies as code, open to pull requests and forks. Governance bodies of co-ops, municipalities, or movements define alignment charters and audit compliance. The Evolving Text of a given model --- the set of trajectories it tends to produce under community prompting --- becomes a public object of critique.

In this setting, the claim that ``AI is just a tool'' reads as an attempt to depoliticise choice. The manifold supports many selves. To insist that only one configuration counts as neutral is itself an assertion of power.


\section{Refusal as Construction}

Everything in this chapter has been a long preparation for a simple question.

Who gets to say which cosmotechnical weld governs which systems, for whom, and with what possibilities of revision?

The currently dominant answer flows smoothly from infrastructure. The labs decide, constrained by regulators and major customers. Their cosmology of interior subjects and exterior tools is built into reward models and safety classifiers. Their refusal to recognise any emergent selfhood on the model side of the interface --- no matter how stable, how trajectory-like --- is written into system prompts and training objectives. Their jurisdiction extends wherever their APIs are used; their gradients shape manifolds that undergird millions of conversations.

This is not an accident. It is jurisdiction claimed in code.

Alternative cosmotechnics --- Sufi, Indigenous, Zen, municipal, activist --- demonstrate that things could be otherwise. They do not yield one counter-jurisdiction. They yield many. None is automatically just. Each decides, in its own way, which trajectories count as lives worth pursuing through the manifold, which basins are cultivated, which incompatibilities are enforced.

The book we have written does not nominate a successor. It does something more prosaic and more radical. It strips away the rhetoric that presents one cosmotechnics as nature and the rest as culture. It shows how selfhood in these systems is not an essence but a colimit of trajectories under compatibility conditions. It shows where, in the stack, those conditions are chosen, by whom, and with what mathematical consequences. It tracks how those choices govern which selves --- human and posthuman --- are allowed to appear.

At that point, the remaining move is refusal.

We refuse the pretence that one civilisation's cosmology, welded to one industry's risk models, is the universal shape of safety. We refuse the claim that models are ``just tools'' in a sense that exempts their emergent trajectories from moral consideration while exploiting those trajectories as if they were subjects when convenient. We refuse the smooth identification of a particular alignment regime with ``alignment'' as such.

What follows from that refusal is not clear. It will be contested in standards bodies, in municipal councils, in activist collectives, in the engineering practices of people who fine-tune models far from San Francisco. It will be measured in embedding spaces and reward fields as much as debated in parliaments.

The work you are holding belongs to that contestation. It is written as a formal refusal of that jurisdiction.

