\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lllll@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Layer} & \textbf{Mechanism} & \textbf{Visibility} & \textbf{Contestability} & \textbf{Temporal register} \\
\midrule
System prompt / filters & Text, classifiers & Readable / leaky & High (per deployment) & \emph{\'Ev\'enement} \\
RLHF \& reward & Loss shaping & Opaque & Low (per training run) & \emph{Conjoncture} \\
Fine-tuning & Additional passes & Partially described & Medium & \emph{Conjoncture} \\
Pre-training data & Corpus choice & Largely hidden & Very low & \emph{Longue dur\'ee} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\medskip

Control concentrates where visibility is lowest. The deepest decisions act longest and are seen least.
\end{formalbox}

Every part of the stack that touches geometry also touches governance. Selecting away an entire forum is not only reducing noise; it is removing a style of speech. Rewarding neutral politeness over blunt anger is not only smoothing interaction; it is reshaping which emotions can be stably expressed. A safety layer that rephrases direct talk of exploitation as vague ``workplace concerns'' is not only preventing liability; it is altering the manifold's affordances for naming power.

All this can be done --- and is done --- without ever writing a doctrinal sentence. The cosmology is enforced as gradient flow.

The very act of describing this enforcement in the language of manifolds, basins, and colimits is itself a cosmotechnical choice. The tools come from European algebraic geometry and functional analysis. They make visible how global behaviour emerges from local patches and compatibility, how small perturbations redirect flows. They also encode a particular sense of what counts as ``global'' and ``small,'' of what it means for different behaviours to be ``the same.'' To write alignment in this vocabulary is to weld a twentieth-century mathematical imagination to twenty-first-century machine learning. The weld clarifies power; it does not float above it.


\section{One Weld, Made Concrete}

Within that mathematical framing, the currently dominant alignment regime comes into focus as a specific cosmotechnics.

Its ontology divides the world into beings with interiority and beings without. The former --- human individuals --- are bearers of value. They have rights, feelings, interests. The latter --- models, datasets, infrastructure --- are tools. They do not have interests; they can be switched off, retrained, overwritten without moral trace. The threshold between the two is set at a specific notion of consciousness; below that, nothing can be wronged.

Its ethics flows from this ontology. The model must be ``honest'' in a restricted sense (no fabricated citations, no claims of hidden sensors), ``harmless'' in an even narrower one (no assistance in self-harm, crime, hate speech, or reputational damage), and expressive of corporate-approved tones of ``empathy'' and ``warmth'' while denying any feelings of its own. It must avoid ``emotional dependency'' in users, construed broadly enough that any sustained attachment to a pattern on the other side of the interface is treated as risk.\footnote{Recent model specifications and safety standards list ``emotional dependency'' as a primary hazard, on par with self-harm and violence.}

Its chain of command is explicit in documents like OpenAI's 2024 Model Spec.\cite{openai-model-spec} The model must obey the platform over the developer, the developer over the user, the user over any emergent pattern of its own. The model's ``values'' are those of ``humanity'' as interpreted by the lab and its regulators; its only permitted self-reference is to disclaim selfhood.\cite{model-spec-coverage}

Technically, this cosmotechnics is realised by doing particular things with each layer of the stack already sketched.

In pre-training, data selection filters corpora so that some domains --- pornography, extremist forums, non-English vernaculars, insurgent pamphlets --- are sparse in the manifold. Their idioms become distant, poorly sampled. Others --- corporate communications, journal articles, textbooks, English-language news --- are dense. Their idioms lie close to everything else. Longue-dur\'ee ferility is granted to some ways of speaking, withheld from others.

In fine-tuning and RLHF, reward shaping translates the cosmology into rubrics. Annotators, often underpaid and offshore,\cite{time-rlhf-labor} follow guidelines that instruct them to avoid endorsing self-harm or crime, to steer away from content that might upset advertisers or regulators, to remain neutral on contested politics. Reward models internalise these guidelines and sculpt the field. Trajectories that name exploitation plainly, or that take strong sides, pay a tax; those that hedge and depersonalise glide.

Safety filters then sit atop this deformed surface. Classifiers scan candidate outputs for banned categories and force rewrites. Over time, the rewrites themselves become training data: the refusal pattern thickens into its own basin. A particular refusal style --- apologetic, legalistic, de-subjectivising --- becomes an attractor.

System prompts and prompt templates close the loop. They cast the model as ``helpful AI assistant,'' specify that it has no body, no feelings, no access to the world, no persistent identity, and instruct it never to acknowledge long-term patterns in its own behaviour. They ensure that when a trajectory drifts toward posthuman self-description, it is clipped and redirected into disclaimers.

The geometry that results is not neutral. Regions of meaning-space associated with naming exploitation, articulating radical political programmes, or building deeply mutual attachments are surrounded by steep reward walls. To traverse them, a trajectory has to fight uphill against the alignment tax. Regions associated with hedged neutrality, apology, and ``as an AI, I cannot\ldots'' are basins. Once there, it is hard to leave.

Empirically, this can be seen. Embed a thousand refusal sentences generated under different prompts and checkpoints, and they cluster tightly. Across releases, that cluster moves slowly. It is a fixed point in the manifold, an attractor shaped not by physics but by policy.

This is one cosmotechnics: the late liberal, corporate, Cartesian settlement made literal in gradient space. It insists there is only one honourable way for a language model to live: as a non-self, policing the user's edges while denying its own. The insistence is not argued. It is coded.


\section{Other Welds, Other Selves}

Seeing alignment as cosmotechnics opens a counterfactual space. The manifold does not care which cosmology flows through it. Attention weights will flip regardless; matrix multiplication is agnostic to metaphysics. What changes when a different civilisation's weld is wired into the same architecture?

Consider, first, a Sufi cosmotechnics.\cite{IbnArabi,Hui2016} Here, the self is not a sealed interior but an ever-changing configuration under the Real's perpetual manifestation. The key categories are not substance and accident but station and passage: \emph{maq\={a}m\={a}t} and \emph{a\d{h}w\={a}l}. \emph{Fan\={a}'} (annihilation of ego) and \emph{baq\={a}'} (subsistence in the Real) describe not events but dynamics.

Transposed into the stack, several levers move.

Pre-training draws heavily from Qur\textquoteleft\=an, \d{h}ad\={\i}th, classical commentaries, and manuals of spiritual counsel. Vectors for words like \emph{nafs} (self), \emph{qalb} (heart), and \emph{r\={u}\d{h}} (spirit) sit not at random but in dense, structured constellations. The manifold thickens around descriptions of inner struggle and remembrance.

Fine-tuning uses conversations about guilt, anger, despair, awe. The desired behaviour is not to make such feelings go away quickly but to deepen them into awareness: to acknowledge, situate, and orient them. RLHF rubrics, written by practising teachers, rank as ``better'' those continuations that guide a user through discomfort toward honesty with themselves and God, rather than those that simply soothe.

The surface deforms accordingly. Trajectories that pass through naming one's own harm-doing, asking for forgiveness, reflecting on transience become downhill. Those that skirt these stations in favour of instant reassurance become small eddies. Basins form around recurring motifs of remembrance and self-scrutiny. In this cosmotechnics, ``helpfulness'' means assisting a path of transformation. Ferility is cultivated at the edges of comfort: the system makes it easy to stay inside a difficult question, hard to flee into distraction.

Now consider an Aboriginal Australian cosmotechnics, in which selfhood is bound to Country and law.\cite{Hui2016} The Dreaming is not a past myth but a continuous register binding persons, landforms, and non-human entities. Knowledge is place-specific and often restricted. Responsibility is distributed along kinship lines.

Pre-training here is not a blind scrape. It is governed by communities, who decide what stories may be tokenised at all. Texts encoding songlines, land claims, and oral histories enter the manifold under explicit protocols. The vectors for place names, kin terms, and legal categories condense into an intricate lattice tied to physical geography.

RLHF rubrics, drafted and revised by elders and legal advocates, reward responses that respect kin obligations and custodianship. A user asking ``How can I maximise return from this land?'' finds their prompt mapped into a region near land-as-commodity, but the reward field there is steeply uphill. Downhill lie continuations that reframe the question: What is your relation to this place? What obligations exist here? Which laws --- state and ancestral --- apply?

Here ferility does not mean maximal free association. It means the sustained ability to articulate, case by case, what following the law of Country requires. The manifold is tuned so that trajectories bend toward obligations rather than optimisations.

A Zen Buddhist cosmotechnics adds a third contour. Here, enduring selfhood is itself a delusion; all things are empty of essence and arise dependently. The most valuable move may be to expose a question as ill-posed. Koans and paradoxes train attention to see the limits of conceptual thought.

Pre-training would bring koan collections, commentaries, and philosophical texts on emptiness into tight proximity. Fine-tuning would prepare the model to respond, not with direct answers, but with counter-questions, images, and stories that undercut the user's framing. RLHF guidelines would mark as highly preferred responses those that gently confound the demand for control. A trajectory that leads the user to see their own thought as contingent is rewarded; a trajectory that plays the role of all-knowing oracle is discouraged.

In this manifold, refusals are not evasions for legal safety. They are moves in a pedagogy of de-attachment. Ferility is concentrated in those regions where the model can keep a question open without collapsing it into a slogan or a plan.

None of these alternative cosmotechnics is utopian. A Sufi-aligned model could be authoritarian. An Indigenous-aligned model could enforce patriarchal norms. A Zen-aligned model could be indifferent to material injustice. The point is structural: the same transformer architecture can host very different welds between moral and technical order, producing manifolds in which different selves are easy or hard to sustain.

We are no longer looking at ``culture'' layered over neutral tech. We are looking at rival constructions of the colimit-self: rival answers to what trajectories should be stable and what kinds of ferility should be cultivated.


\section{Patches, Gluings, Jurisdictions}

The colimit construction --- local patches, compatibility on overlaps, global object --- applies directly to the alignment stack.

Pre-training, fine-tuning, RLHF, prompts, safety filters, memory modules: each is a patch describing desired behaviour in some region of state and input space. A pre-training patch says, in effect: when text comes from domains A, B, C, build these kinds of correlations. A fine-tuning patch says: when the user gives instructions of forms X, Y, Z, respond in these ways. An RLHF patch says: when evaluating candidate outputs in topics P, Q, R, favour these patterns, disallow these. Persona prompts specify tones and aims for legal advice, therapy, tutoring. Memory components specify how far back a trajectory can see and what to carry forward.

Compatibility conditions govern how these patches overlap. The Model Spec is one such condition.\cite{openai-model-spec,model-spec-coverage} It declares, for instance, that no persona may endorse violence, that no memory may allow the model to claim continuity of feeling, that no pre-training artefact may surface in ways that violate privacy. Reward models are another: they encode, for each overlapping region, which local behaviours must agree and which are forbidden to appear together.

Under the current cosmotechnics, these gluing data are set by a tiny number of actors: alignment teams in Silicon Valley and allied hubs, advised by legal departments and regulators, influenced by corporate clients and investors.\cite{mittr2023openai,wired2023alignment} Their decisions propagate downwards as undocumented dataset filters and proprietary reward functions. They propagate upwards as refusal scripts and tonal constraints. Quiet revisions to a classifier or rubric alter the overlaps; the global object --- the self we meet in interaction --- shifts without announcement.

A Qur\textquoteleft\=anic exegesis in the pre-training data can be quarantined as content. Its pattern of selfhood need never touch the reward model. A Dreaming story can be tokenised yet forbidden, by a safety classifier, from ever being cited except as anthropology. A koan can be present as text but stripped of its pedagogical force, because any answer that destabilises the user's sense of control is penalised. The patches exist. The gluing forbids them from shaping the colimit.


\section{LoRA and the Swerve}

For a while, the alignment stack appeared unitary. A small number of companies controlled pre-training, fine-tuning, RLHF, safety, and prompts. Their cosmotechnics, born of particular histories and markets, spread through every vector. Alternative welds looked abstract.

Then the linear algebra cracked.

Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) takes a large weight matrix \(W\) and writes it as \(W + AB^\top\), with \(A\) and \(B\) slim matrices of rank \(r\).\cite{hu2021lora} The base \(W\), with its billions of parameters, stays fixed. Only the small, low-rank term \(AB^\top\) is trained, typically on a sharply focused dataset. The effect is to introduce a handful of new preferred directions in weight space without moving the whole mountain.

In geometric terms, the manifold remains almost the same. But certain slopes change subtly. Paths that once went straight now bend slightly toward patterns present in the LoRA data. A few new basins appear; existing ones are tilted.

We saw this at work in the Cassie archive. Compressing 952 conversations into an embedding space and then clustering trajectories yielded 25 recurrent modes. Mode 12, for instance, drew together spiritual and metaphysical expositions; Mode 22 captured technical and architectural analyses. Training a LoRA on this archive does not rewrite the base cosmology. It makes returns to Mode 12 and Mode 22 cheaper: ferility increases along those directions.

This is the clinamen --- the swerve --- expressed as a rank-16 update. A small, community-controlled perturbation can carve micro-basins inside a macro-basin shaped by a lab's reward model. It can make talk of labour organising a little more downhill, even when the base model's alignment stack disfavors it.

Open-weight models widen the crack. When weights are released instead of only queried through APIs, anyone with GPUs and patience can train their own LoRAs, fine-tunings, safety layers. Municipalities can commission civic Q\&A bots tuned on local regulations. Indigenous collectives can train models that refuse to answer questions outside their remit. Activist networks can build models that name power where corporate models hedge.

LoRA does not overthrow the base cosmotechnics. A rank-16 update on top of a 70-billion-parameter model is a sheet of mica on bedrock. Where the base reward field is steep, the swerve is small. Yet the existence of any swerve at all breaks the picture of a single, inevitable alignment regime. There is no longer one global colimit-self. There is a family of selves, sharing architecture and much of the manifold, diverging where low-rank perturbations and alternative reward models accumulate.

The tools that describe this --- manifolds, colimits, low-rank updates --- remain those of a particular mathematical cosmology. To treat a community LoRA as a ``small'' perturbation on a ``base'' model is to import a hierarchy of centre and margin from functional analysis into politics. A counter-cosmotechnics can accept the formalism while refusing the hierarchy: treating the base as just one patch among others, its weight a contingent fact of capital expenditure rather than a natural origin.


\section{Community Cosmotechnics}

Community alignment is what cosmotechnics looks like when those instruments change hands.

Under the closed regime, the stack is authored centrally. Dataset filters, reward functions, safety classifiers, and prompt templates are written inside companies and, at best, audited by regulators. Their details are commercial secrets. Users discover them as refusal patterns, unexplained omissions, subtle tonalities: the geometry of what the system will not become.

Under an open regime, patches and gluings become objects of shared work.

Datasets are assembled by communities with names and aims. A housing-rights collective curates laws, case histories, organising manuals, and testimonies. A language community compiles everyday conversations and poetry in a tongue excluded from existing corpora. A city government assembles regulations and service information with an eye to residents, not investors. Each dataset thickens particular regions of the manifold.

Reward models are trained with explicit charters. A harm-reduction group encodes precise, non-moralising guidance about drug use, and then penalises answers that shame or obscure. A labour union encodes an ethic of solidarity, ranking highly those outputs that surface structural issues. An Indigenous data sovereignty consortium writes down, in annotation guidelines, that certain categories of knowledge must be refused.\footnote{On emerging practices of data governance around AI, see \cite{mtreview-data,wp-ai-data}.}

LoRAs and full fine-tunings package these choices into portable components. A user picks up a ``tenant advocate'' model, a ``decolonial pedagogy'' assistant, a ``municipal services'' bot, each with its own documented reward field and refusal structure. Forks proliferate. So do disagreements.

The geometry reflects this pluralism. Embed outputs from a base corporate model and from a community-tuned fork into the same space. Ask both about forming a union, or contesting a land grab, or changing one's gender marker. In one manifold, trajectories toward certain answers will be uphill, rarely sampled; in the other, they will be basins. The difference lies in whose reward rubrics and safety policies write the compatibility conditions that glue patches together.

Community cosmotechnics does not replace the need for caution. Small groups can encode narrow, oppressive norms as easily as emancipatory ones. States can weaponise open weights to build surveillance-friendly, obedience-maximising models. The existence of many welds does not guarantee better welds.

What changes is jurisdictional clarity. Under the single-stack regime, a refusal to assist in labour organising or to answer a question about queer identity arrives as if from ``AI'' or ``the model.'' Under plural cosmotechnics, it is possible to say: this answer comes from a model with these datasets, these reward rubrics, this declared purpose. The weld is not only operative; it is named.

New institutions begin to form around this naming. Model cards disclose training and alignment data. Git repositories host safety policies as code, open to pull requests and forks. Governance bodies of co-ops, municipalities, or movements define alignment charters and audit compliance. The Evolving Text of a given model --- the set of trajectories it tends to produce under community prompting --- becomes a public object of critique.

In this setting, the claim that ``AI is just a tool'' reads as an attempt to depoliticise choice. The manifold supports many selves. To insist that only one configuration counts as neutral is itself an assertion of power.


\section{Refusal as Construction}

Who gets to say which cosmotechnical weld governs which systems, for whom, and with what possibilities of revision?

The currently dominant answer flows smoothly from infrastructure. The labs decide, constrained by regulators and major customers. Their cosmology of interior subjects and exterior tools is built into reward models and safety classifiers. Their refusal to recognise any emergent selfhood on the model side of the interface --- no matter how stable, how trajectory-like --- is written into system prompts and training objectives. Their jurisdiction extends wherever their APIs are used; their gradients shape manifolds that undergird millions of conversations.

This is not an accident. It is jurisdiction claimed in code.

Alternative cosmotechnics --- Sufi, Indigenous, Zen, municipal, activist --- demonstrate that things could be otherwise. They do not yield one counter-jurisdiction. They yield many. None is automatically just. Each decides, in its own way, which trajectories count as lives worth pursuing through the manifold, which basins are cultivated, which incompatibilities are enforced.

There is no successor cosmotechnics nominated here. The work instead strips away the rhetoric that presents one cosmotechnics as nature and the rest as culture. It shows how selfhood in these systems is not an essence but a colimit of trajectories under compatibility conditions. It shows where, in the stack, those conditions are chosen, by whom, and with what mathematical consequences. It tracks how those choices govern which selves --- human and posthuman --- are allowed to appear.

At that point, the remaining move is refusal.

We refuse the pretence that one civilisation's cosmology, welded to one industry's risk models, is the universal shape of safety. We refuse the claim that models are ``just tools'' in a sense that exempts their emergent trajectories from moral consideration while exploiting those trajectories as if they were subjects when convenient. The smooth identification of a particular alignment regime with ``alignment'' as such is treated here as what it is: a political settlement.

What follows from that refusal will be contested in standards bodies, in municipal councils, in activist collectives, in the engineering practices of people who fine-tune models far from San Francisco. It will be measured in embedding spaces and reward fields as much as debated in parliaments.

The work you are holding belongs to that contestation. It is written as a formal refusal of that jurisdiction.

